According to all projection variants used, the size of the working age population (aged 15–59)
will be considerably larger than in 2021, as well as the ‘elderly’ population 60+ years. Therefore the
population will grow older, regardless of which projection is used, as is expressed in the median
age, which will increase from 21.6 years in 2021 to over 30 years, according to the low fertility
variants.
